  "independent_facts": {
    "initial_native_host_knowledge": "Management initialization zeros its local remote AP cache at +0x108. A cold own HOST B20/fresh exact B20 reply supplies known remote20; type-B dispatch and handleRemotePowerState publish that low word and wake waiters.",
    "retained_native_skip": "Parent ON1 maps to AP wire20. _signalApPowerGated compares that wire state to the same cached remote +0x108 and returns success before constructing/sending/waiting when already equal. A skip obtains no new HOST reply.",
    "cache_and_IOP_are_separate": "Management object +0x108 is neither parent RTBuddy hostflag byte +0x108 nor firmware internal AP state33. Type-7 Running20 updates parent IOP status8; the complete ACK handler has no remote AP-cache store.",
    "native_route_order": "Complete parent change calls notification(new,current) before the perform route, then notification(current,current) after transition. ON1 from Sleep2 gets no pre-ON AP signal and its post-ON callback1/1 takes the cached20 skip. The management callback preserves +0x108; its watchdog reset fields +0x10c/+0x110/+0x118 differ.",
    "retained_target2": "Management callback2/1 passes parent2 to AP signaling, which returns invalid argument 0xe00002c7 without sending. The callback ignores that return and quiesces the watchdog. Perform2 passes the unchanged target2 to the separate type-6 request table, selecting202. Callback2/2 has no AP signal.",
    "endpoint_reuse": "The ON perform body loads parent management endpoint +0x21f0 and, when nonnull, branches around creating/initializing a new management endpoint. The inspected retained route does not itself clear the AP cache. Runtime route selection, alternate providers, endpoint destruction elsewhere and native object state remain unobserved.",
    "first202_not_missing_parent_OFF": "A direct management202 corresponds to native retained target2 behavior. Native full parentOFF0 is different: pre-OFF callback can send HOST B201, and its management request table selects type6/201. Physical PMGR OFF in our successful202 experiment is not proof of native full parentOFF0 or AP OFF0."
  },
