  "prior_experimental_assumption_correction": "The earlier v10 requirement for a fresh own B20 reply after every Running20 was a protocol hypothesis. Native code conditionally skips the message when remote20 is already known. The actual duplicate-state panic refutes unconditional B20 for this retained trial. Frozen historical reports are preserved.",
  "next_candidate_hypothesis": "Carry only an explicitly kernel-bound own cold HOST B20/fresh exact reply under the same owner and consumer, preserve its state through the successful first management202/OFF, observe fresh HELLO/maps/Running20 after qualified reentry, and suppress duplicate HOST B20. Then test the existing exact management202/shutdown-ACK/checked-stop/paired-OFF boundary. This is future fresh-boot qualification and trial work, not established repeatable recovery.",
  "no_new_HOST_reply_for_skip": true,
